IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc3-periods`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 3 (claimant treated as occupying or not occupying accommodation).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- WHAT THIS SCHEDULE DECIDES. Regulation 25 asks whether the claimant meets the occupation condition. Part 1 says which accommodation a claimant is
-- treated as occupying: the home they normally occupy (paragraph 1), plus six situations in which they are treated as occupying something else, or
-- two homes, or a home before they have moved into it. Part 2 (paragraph 9) says when a temporary absence ends the occupation.
-- Each paragraph is a rule over its own record of facts. "The payment condition and the liability condition" are regulation 25(5) (piece uc1) and
-- are stated inputs. Where the text bounds a situation by a period of months, the periods module counts the months (fork U3-F8).
--
-- WHEN THE MONTH STARTS. Paragraphs 5(4), 6(4), 7(3) and 8(2) say "for more than one month" / "for more than 12 months" without saying from when.
-- Each record carries the first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying the accommodation under that paragraph, and the day the
-- question is asked about (fork U3-F19, assumed and not ruled).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 1: the general rule.
-- src:2055 | (1) The general rule is that a claimant is to be treated as occupying as their home the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home.
-- src:2056 | (2) Subject to the following provisions of this Part, no claimant is to be treated as occupying accommodation which comprises more than one dwelling.
-- src:2057 | (3) Where none of those provisions applies and the claimant occupies more than one dwelling, regard is to be had to all the circumstances in determining which dwelling the claimant normally occupies as their home, including (among other things) any persons with whom the claimant occupies each dwelling.
@ref Sch 3 para 1(1) to (3) (src:2055-2057)
DECLARE `Accommodation the claimant may occupy as their home` HAS
    -- sub-paragraph (3): where the claimant occupies more than one dwelling, all the circumstances decide which dwelling is normally occupied,
    -- including (among other things) any persons with whom the claimant occupies each dwelling; the answer is this input
    `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- sub-paragraph (4): "dwelling" is a dwelling within the meaning of Part 1 (England and Wales) or Part 2 (Scotland) of the Local Government Finance Act 1992
    `number of dwellings the accommodation comprises`                                                IS A NUMBER

-- src:2055 | (1) The general rule is that a claimant is to be treated as occupying as their home the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home.
-- src:2056 | (2) Subject to the following provisions of this Part, no claimant is to be treated as occupying accommodation which comprises more than one dwelling.
@ref Sch 3 para 1(1) and (2) (src:2055-2056)
GIVEN accommodation IS A `Accommodation the claimant may occupy as their home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 1 — the claimant is treated as occupying the accommodation as their home` accommodation MEANS
    (accommodation's `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home`)
    AND (accommodation's `number of dwellings the accommodation comprises` AT MOST 1)

-- Paragraph 2: croft land used for the purposes of the accommodation is treated as included in it.
-- src:2062 | (1) Where accommodation which a claimant normally occupies as their home is situated on or pertains to a croft, croft land used for the purposes of the accommodation is to be treated as included in the accommodation.
-- src:2063 | (2) “Croft” means a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993 .
@ref Sch 3 para 2 (src:2062-2063)
DECLARE `Accommodation that may be on a croft` HAS
    `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation`                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2062 | (1) Where accommodation which a claimant normally occupies as their home is situated on or pertains to a croft, croft land used for the purposes of the accommodation is to be treated as included in the accommodation.
@ref Sch 3 para 2(1) (src:2062)
GIVEN accommodation IS A `Accommodation that may be on a croft`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 2 — the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation` accommodation MEANS
    (accommodation's `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home`)
    AND (accommodation's `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993`)
    AND (accommodation's `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 3: living in other accommodation during essential repairs.
-- src:2065 | (1) Where a claimant—
-- src:2066 | (a) is required to move into accommodation (“the other accommodation”) on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home;
-- src:2067 | (b) intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair; and
-- src:2068 | (c) meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of either the other accommodation or the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (but not both),
-- src:2069 | the claimant is to be treated as normally occupying as their home the accommodation in respect of which those conditions are met.
@ref Sch 3 para 3 (src:2065-2069)
DECLARE `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 3` IS ONE OF
    `the other accommodation`
    `the accommodation under repair`
    `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`

-- src:2065 | (1) Where a claimant—
-- src:2066 | (a) is required to move into accommodation (“the other accommodation”) on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home;
-- src:2067 | (b) intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair; and
-- src:2068 | (c) meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of either the other accommodation or the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (but not both),
-- src:2069 | the claimant is to be treated as normally occupying as their home the accommodation in respect of which those conditions are met.
-- src:2070 | (2) A claimant is subject to the general rule in paragraph 1 where—
-- src:2071 | (a) sub-paragraph (1)(a) and (b) apply to the claimant; but
-- src:2072 | (b) the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both the other accommodation and the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home.
@ref Sch 3 para 3 (src:2065-2072)
DECLARE `Claimant living in other accommodation during essential repairs` HAS
    `the claimant is required to move into the other accommodation on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2065 | (1) Where a claimant—
@ref Sch 3 para 3(1)(a) and (b) (src:2065-2067)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation during essential repairs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 3(1)(a) and (b) — the claimant moved out for essential repairs and intends to return` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `the claimant is required to move into the other accommodation on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair`)

-- src:2065 | (1) Where a claimant—
-- src:2066 | (a) is required to move into accommodation (“the other accommodation”) on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home;
-- src:2067 | (b) intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair; and
-- src:2068 | (c) meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of either the other accommodation or the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (but not both),
-- src:2069 | the claimant is to be treated as normally occupying as their home the accommodation in respect of which those conditions are met.
-- src:2070 | (2) A claimant is subject to the general rule in paragraph 1 where—
-- src:2071 | (a) sub-paragraph (1)(a) and (b) apply to the claimant; but
-- src:2072 | (b) the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both the other accommodation and the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home.
@ref Sch 3 para 3(1) and (2) (src:2065-2072)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation during essential repairs`
GIVETH A `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 3`
`Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` claimant MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Sch 3 para 3(1)(a) and (b) — the claimant moved out for essential repairs and intends to return` claimant) THEN `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`
        IF (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`) AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home`) THEN `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`
        IF claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation` THEN `the other accommodation`
        IF claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home` THEN `the accommodation under repair`
        OTHERWISE `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`

