-- Paragraph 4: housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing; both are treated as the single accommodation normally occupied.
-- src:2074 | (1) In sub-paragraph (2), “relevant claimant” means a claimant who meets all of the following conditions—
-- src:2075 | (a) the first condition is that the claimant has been housed in two dwellings (“accommodation A” and “accommodation B”) by a provider of social housing on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with the claimant;
-- src:2076 | (b) the second condition is that the claimant normally occupies both accommodation A and accommodation B with children or qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible;
-- src:2077 | (c) the third condition is that the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both accommodation A and accommodation B (and for these purposes it is irrelevant whether the claimant's liability is to the same or a different person).
-- src:2078 | (2) In the case of a relevant claimant, both accommodation A and accommodation B are to be treated as the single accommodation which the relevant claimant normally occupies as their home.
-- src:2079 | (3) In sub-paragraph (1), “provider of social housing” has the meaning given in paragraph 2 of Schedule 4.
@ref Sch 3 para 4 (src:2074-2079)
DECLARE `Claimant housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing` HAS
    `the provider of social housing that housed the claimant`                                                              IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
    `the claimant has been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with the claimant`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `the claimant normally occupies both accommodation A and accommodation B with children or qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation A`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation B`                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2074 | (1) In sub-paragraph (2), “relevant claimant” means a claimant who meets all of the following conditions—
-- src:2075 | (a) the first condition is that the claimant has been housed in two dwellings (“accommodation A” and “accommodation B”) by a provider of social housing on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with the claimant;
-- src:2076 | (b) the second condition is that the claimant normally occupies both accommodation A and accommodation B with children or qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible;
-- src:2077 | (c) the third condition is that the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both accommodation A and accommodation B (and for these purposes it is irrelevant whether the claimant's liability is to the same or a different person).
-- src:2078 | (2) In the case of a relevant claimant, both accommodation A and accommodation B are to be treated as the single accommodation which the relevant claimant normally occupies as their home.
@ref Sch 3 para 4(1) and (2) (src:2074-2078)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` claimant MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (claimant's `the provider of social housing that housed the claimant`))
    AND (claimant's `the claimant has been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with the claimant`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant normally occupies both accommodation A and accommodation B with children or qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation A`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation B`)

