GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 5(3) — a person is specified` person MEANS
    (person's `a claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible`)
    AND (`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (person's payments))

-- Paragraph 5: moving home, with the new home adapted for a disabled person. The old and the new accommodation are both treated as occupied for up to one month.
-- src:2081 | (1) Sub-paragraph (2) applies where—
-- src:2082 | (a) the claimant has moved into accommodation (“the new accommodation”) and, immediately before the move, met the payment condition and liability condition in respect of the new accommodation; and
-- src:2083 | (b) there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a person specified in sub-paragraph (3).
-- src:2084 | (2) The claimant is to be treated as occupying both the new accommodation and the accommodation from which the move was made (“the old accommodation”) if—
-- src:2085 | (a) immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation; and
-- src:2086 | (b) the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable.
-- src:2087 | (3) A person is specified in this sub-paragraph if the person is—
-- src:2088 | (a) a claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible; and
-- src:2089 | (b) in receipt of—
-- src:2090 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate,
-- src:2091 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations,
-- src:2092 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025,
-- src:2093 | (ii) attendance allowance, ...
-- src:2094 | (iia) pension age disability payment,
-- src:2095 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment or
-- src:2096 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate
-- src:2097 | (4) No claimant may be treated as occupying both the old accommodation and the new accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
@ref Sch 3 para 5 (src:2081-2097)
DECLARE `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person` HAS
    `the claimant has moved into the new accommodation`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `immediately before the move, the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the new accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a specified person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the specified person`                                                                                                 IS A `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)`
    `immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations`                                         IS A DATE
    `day to which the question relates`                                                                                    IS A DATE

-- src:2081 | (1) Sub-paragraph (2) applies where—
-- src:2082 | (a) the claimant has moved into accommodation (“the new accommodation”) and, immediately before the move, met the payment condition and liability condition in respect of the new accommodation; and
-- src:2083 | (b) there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a person specified in sub-paragraph (3).
@ref Sch 3 para 5(1) (src:2081-2083)
GIVEN move IS A `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 5(1) — sub-paragraph (2) applies` move MEANS
    (move's `the claimant has moved into the new accommodation`)
    AND (move's `immediately before the move, the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the new accommodation`)
    AND (move's `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a specified person`)
    AND (`Sch 3 para 5(3) — a person is specified` (move's `the specified person`))

-- src:2084 | (2) The claimant is to be treated as occupying both the new accommodation and the accommodation from which the move was made (“the old accommodation”) if—
-- src:2085 | (a) immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation; and
-- src:2086 | (b) the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable.
@ref Sch 3 para 5(2) (src:2084-2086)
GIVEN move IS A `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 5(2) — conditions for being treated as occupying both` move MEANS
    (`Sch 3 para 5(1) — sub-paragraph (2) applies` move)
    AND (move's `immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation`)
    AND (move's `the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable`)

-- src:2084 | (2) The claimant is to be treated as occupying both the new accommodation and the accommodation from which the move was made (“the old accommodation”) if—
-- src:2085 | (a) immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation; and
-- src:2086 | (b) the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable.
-- src:2097 | (4) No claimant may be treated as occupying both the old accommodation and the new accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
@ref Sch 3 para 5(2) and (4) (src:2084-2086) (src:2097)
GIVEN move IS A `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` move MEANS
    (`Sch 3 para 5(2) — conditions for being treated as occupying both` move)
    AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (move's `day to which the question relates`) (move's `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations`) 1)

