-- Paragraph 6: living in other accommodation because of a reasonable fear of violence.
-- src:2099 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2100 | (a) a claimant is occupying accommodation (“the other accommodation”) other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (“the home accommodation”); and
-- src:2101 | (b) it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible; but
-- src:2102 | (c) the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation.
@ref Sch 3 para 6(1) (src:2099-2102)
DECLARE `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 6` IS ONE OF
    `both the home accommodation and the other accommodation`
    `the home accommodation only`
    `the other accommodation only`
    `neither: paragraph 6 does not treat the claimant as occupying either`
    `not covered: the text does not say which accommodation the claimant is treated as occupying once the 12 months of paragraph 6(4) have passed`

-- src:2099 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2100 | (a) a claimant is occupying accommodation (“the other accommodation”) other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (“the home accommodation”); and
-- src:2101 | (b) it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible; but
-- src:2102 | (c) the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation.
-- src:2103 | (2) The claimant is to be treated as normally occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation as their home if—
-- src:2104 | (a) the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both the home accommodation and other accommodation; and
-- src:2105 | (b) it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation.
-- src:2106 | (3) Where the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of one accommodation only, the claimant is to be treated as normally occupying that accommodation as their home but only if it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of that accommodation.
-- src:2107 | (4) No claimant may be treated as occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under sub-paragraph (2) for more than 12 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 6 (src:2099-2107)
DECLARE `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence` HAS
    `the claimant is occupying accommodation other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the home accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the other accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations`                                         IS A DATE
    `day to which the question relates`                                                                                    IS A DATE

-- src:2099 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2100 | (a) a claimant is occupying accommodation (“the other accommodation”) other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (“the home accommodation”); and
-- src:2101 | (b) it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible; but
-- src:2102 | (c) the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation.
@ref Sch 3 para 6(1) (src:2099-2102)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `the claimant is occupying accommodation other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home`)
    AND (claimant's `it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation`)

-- src:2103 | (2) The claimant is to be treated as normally occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation as their home if—
-- src:2104 | (a) the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both the home accommodation and other accommodation; and
-- src:2105 | (b) it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation.
-- src:2107 | (4) No claimant may be treated as occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under sub-paragraph (2) for more than 12 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 6(2) and (4) (src:2103-2105) (src:2107)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 6(2) — the claimant is treated as normally occupying both` claimant MEANS
    (`Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` claimant)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`)
    AND (claimant's `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the home accommodation`)
    AND (claimant's `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the other accommodation`)
    AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (claimant's `day to which the question relates`) (claimant's `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations`) 12)

-- src:2106 | (3) Where the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of one accommodation only, the claimant is to be treated as normally occupying that accommodation as their home but only if it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of that accommodation.
@ref Sch 3 para 6(3) (src:2106)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence`
GIVETH A `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 6`
`Sch 3 para 6(3) — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying where one only meets the conditions` claimant MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` claimant) AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation`) AND (NOT (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`)) AND (claimant's `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the home accommodation`) THEN `the home accommodation only`
        IF (`Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` claimant) AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`) AND (NOT (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation`)) AND (claimant's `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the other accommodation`) THEN `the other accommodation only`
        OTHERWISE `neither: paragraph 6 does not treat the claimant as occupying either`

-- Paragraph 6(4): the same conditions as (2), but the 12 months have passed. The text says that no claimant may be treated as occupying both for more than
-- 12 months, and not what the claimant is treated as occupying after that (fork U3-F20): the answer is the explicit not-covered value.
-- src:2107 | (4) No claimant may be treated as occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under sub-paragraph (2) for more than 12 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 6(4) (src:2107)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 6(4) — the 12 months have passed on conditions that would otherwise treat the claimant as occupying both` claimant MEANS
    (`Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` claimant)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation`)
    AND (claimant's `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the home accommodation`)
    AND (claimant's `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the other accommodation`)
    AND (NOT (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (claimant's `day to which the question relates`) (claimant's `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations`) 12))

-- src:2099 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2100 | (a) a claimant is occupying accommodation (“the other accommodation”) other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home (“the home accommodation”); and
-- src:2101 | (b) it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible; but
-- src:2102 | (c) the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation.
-- src:2103 | (2) The claimant is to be treated as normally occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation as their home if—
-- src:2104 | (a) the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of both the home accommodation and other accommodation; and
-- src:2105 | (b) it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation.
-- src:2106 | (3) Where the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of one accommodation only, the claimant is to be treated as normally occupying that accommodation as their home but only if it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of that accommodation.
-- src:2107 | (4) No claimant may be treated as occupying both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under sub-paragraph (2) for more than 12 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 6 (src:2099-2107)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence`
GIVETH A `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 6`
`Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` claimant MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Sch 3 para 6(2) — the claimant is treated as normally occupying both` claimant THEN `both the home accommodation and the other accommodation`
        IF `Sch 3 para 6(4) — the 12 months have passed on conditions that would otherwise treat the claimant as occupying both` claimant THEN `not covered: the text does not say which accommodation the claimant is treated as occupying once the 12 months of paragraph 6(4) have passed`
        OTHERWISE `Sch 3 para 6(3) — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying where one only meets the conditions` claimant

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 7: moving in delayed by adaptations to meet disablement needs; treated as having occupied before moving in, for up to one month.
-- src:2109 | (1) The claimant is to be treated as having occupied accommodation before they moved into it where—
-- src:2110 | (a) the claimant has since moved in and, immediately before the move, met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation;
-- src:2111 | (b) there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person; and
-- src:2112 | (c) it was reasonable to delay moving in.
-- src:2113 | (2) “Relevant person” means a person specified in paragraph 5(3).
-- src:2114 | (3) No claimant may be treated as occupying accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
@ref Sch 3 para 7 (src:2109-2114)
DECLARE `Move that was delayed by adaptations to accommodation` HAS
    `the claimant has since moved in`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person`                                                                                               IS A `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)`
    `it was reasonable to delay moving in`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation`                                  IS A DATE
    `day to which the question relates`                                                                                 IS A DATE

-- src:2109 | (1) The claimant is to be treated as having occupied accommodation before they moved into it where—
-- src:2110 | (a) the claimant has since moved in and, immediately before the move, met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation;
-- src:2111 | (b) there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person; and
-- src:2112 | (c) it was reasonable to delay moving in.
-- src:2113 | (2) “Relevant person” means a person specified in paragraph 5(3).
-- src:2114 | (3) No claimant may be treated as occupying accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
@ref Sch 3 para 7 (src:2109-2114)
GIVEN move IS A `Move that was delayed by adaptations to accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` move MEANS
    (move's `the claimant has since moved in`)
    AND (move's `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation`)
    AND (move's `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person`)
    AND (`Sch 3 para 5(3) — a person is specified` (move's `the relevant person`))
    AND (move's `it was reasonable to delay moving in`)
    AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (move's `day to which the question relates`) (move's `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation`) 1)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 8: moving in following a stay in hospital or a care home; treated as having occupied before moving in, for up to one month.
-- "Patient": a person undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution (paragraph 8(3)).
-- "Care home": Schedule 1 paragraph 1.
-- src:2118 | (b) the liability to make the payments arose while the claimant was a patient or accommodated in a care home (or, in the case of a joint claim, while both joint claimants were patients or were accommodated in a care home).
-- src:2122 | “patient” means a person who is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution.
@ref Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) and (3) (src:2118) (src:2122)
DECLARE `Person's situation when a liability arose` HAS
    `the person was undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the care home in which the person was accommodated`                                                                 IS A `Premises that may be a care home`
    `the person was accommodated in that care home`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2118 | (b) the liability to make the payments arose while the claimant was a patient or accommodated in a care home (or, in the case of a joint claim, while both joint claimants were patients or were accommodated in a care home).
-- src:2119 | (2) No claimant may be treated as occupying the accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
-- src:2120 | (3) In this paragraph—
-- src:2121 | “care home” has the meaning given in paragraph 1 of Schedule 1;
-- src:2122 | “patient” means a person who is undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution.
@ref Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) and (3) (src:2118) (src:2121-2122)
GIVEN situation IS A `Person's situation when a liability arose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` situation MEANS
    (situation's `the person was undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution`)
    OR ((situation's `the person was accommodated in that care home`) AND (`Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (situation's `the care home in which the person was accommodated`)))

-- src:2115 | 8 Moving into accommodation following stay in hospital or care home
-- src:2116 | (1) The claimant is to be treated as having occupied accommodation before they moved into it where—
-- src:2117 | (a) the claimant has since moved in and, immediately before the move, met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of that accommodation; and
-- src:2118 | (b) the liability to make the payments arose while the claimant was a patient or accommodated in a care home (or, in the case of a joint claim, while both joint claimants were patients or were accommodated in a care home).
-- src:2119 | (2) No claimant may be treated as occupying the accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
@ref Sch 3 para 8 (src:2115-2119)
DECLARE `Move following a stay in hospital or a care home` HAS
    `the claimant has since moved in`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim basis`                                                                                                       IS A `Claim basis`
    `the situation of the claimant when the liability to make the payments arose`                                      IS A `Person's situation when a liability arose`
    `the situation of the other joint claimant when the liability to make the payments arose`                          IS A `Person's situation when a liability arose`
    `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation`                                  IS A DATE
    `day to which the question relates`                                                                                 IS A DATE

-- src:2118 | (b) the liability to make the payments arose while the claimant was a patient or accommodated in a care home (or, in the case of a joint claim, while both joint claimants were patients or were accommodated in a care home).
@ref Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) (src:2118)
GIVEN move IS A `Move following a stay in hospital or a care home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the liability arose while the claimant (or both joint claimants) were patients or in a care home` move MEANS
    IF (move's `claim basis`) EQUALS `joint claimants`
    THEN (`Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (move's `the situation of the claimant when the liability to make the payments arose`)) AND (`Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (move's `the situation of the other joint claimant when the liability to make the payments arose`))
    ELSE `Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (move's `the situation of the claimant when the liability to make the payments arose`)

-- src:2116 | (1) The claimant is to be treated as having occupied accommodation before they moved into it where—
-- src:2117 | (a) the claimant has since moved in and, immediately before the move, met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of that accommodation; and
-- src:2118 | (b) the liability to make the payments arose while the claimant was a patient or accommodated in a care home (or, in the case of a joint claim, while both joint claimants were patients or were accommodated in a care home).
-- src:2119 | (2) No claimant may be treated as occupying the accommodation under this paragraph for more than one month.
@ref Sch 3 para 8(1) and (2) (src:2116-2119)
GIVEN move IS A `Move following a stay in hospital or a care home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` move MEANS
    (move's `the claimant has since moved in`)
    AND (move's `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation`)
    AND (`Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the liability arose while the claimant (or both joint claimants) were patients or in a care home` move)
    AND (`uc3 — a day falls within the first months after a start day` (move's `day to which the question relates`) (move's `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation`) 1)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2, paragraph 9: a temporary absence that exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months ends the occupation, except for a claimant who falls
-- within paragraph 3 (sub-paragraph (2)) and, for a claimant who falls within paragraph 6, where the period is 12 months (sub-paragraph (3)).
-- src:2125 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3), a claimant is to be treated as no longer occupying accommodation from which they are temporarily absent where the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months.
-- src:2126 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) does not apply to a claimant who falls within paragraph 3.
-- src:2127 | (3) Where a claimant who falls within paragraph 6 is temporarily absent from the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home, the claimant is to be treated as no longer occupying that accommodation where the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 12 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 9 (src:2125-2127)
DECLARE `Temporary absence from accommodation` HAS
    `first day of the absence`                                                                    IS A DATE
    `day to which the question relates`                                                           IS A DATE
    `last day to which the absence is expected to last`                                           IS A DATE
    `the claimant falls within paragraph 3`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant falls within paragraph 6`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2125 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3), a claimant is to be treated as no longer occupying accommodation from which they are temporarily absent where the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 9(1) (src:2125)
GIVEN absence IS A `Temporary absence from accommodation`
      `number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 9 — the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, a number of months` absence `number of months` MEANS
    (`uc3 — a period lasting to a last day exceeds a number of months` (absence's `first day of the absence`) (absence's `day to which the question relates`) `number of months`)
    OR (`uc3 — a period lasting to a last day exceeds a number of months` (absence's `first day of the absence`) (absence's `last day to which the absence is expected to last`) `number of months`)

-- src:2125 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3), a claimant is to be treated as no longer occupying accommodation from which they are temporarily absent where the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months.
-- src:2126 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) does not apply to a claimant who falls within paragraph 3.
-- src:2127 | (3) Where a claimant who falls within paragraph 6 is temporarily absent from the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home, the claimant is to be treated as no longer occupying that accommodation where the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 12 months.
@ref Sch 3 para 9 (src:2125-2127)
GIVEN absence IS A `Temporary absence from accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` absence MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF absence's `the claimant falls within paragraph 3` THEN FALSE
        IF absence's `the claimant falls within paragraph 6` THEN `Sch 3 para 9 — the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, a number of months` absence 12
        OTHERWISE `Sch 3 para 9 — the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, a number of months` absence 6
